        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Judging by the text of this issue, what you actually want is to surround the entire *line* and not sentence.\r\nVim (and Neovim, of course) has a motion for lines which is coded with [`_`](https://vimhelp.org/motion.txt.html#_) (underscore). So to surround the entire line with parenthesis, type `sa_)` (`ys_)` in your setup). You can make your own keymap for `yss` to mimic `ys_`.\r\n\r\nBy the way, Vim also has a text object for a [`sentence`](https://vimhelp.org/motion.txt.html#as).",
