            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> How can I setup a linewise surround to `yss`. I tried but it didn't work:\r\n> \r\n> ```viml\r\n>   config = function()\r\n>     require 'mini.surround'.setup()\r\n>     vim.api.nvim_set_keymap('n', 'yss', 'ys_', {noremap = false, silent = true})\r\n>   end,\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nBy default 'mini.surround' has different from 'tpope/vim-surround' mappings. See [this part of the help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d8bab386fe69c02129857957e148c7178bf94ae9/doc/mini-surround.txt#L500-L522).\r\n\r\nIf, by any chance, you still want to have `yss` to surround the line while having default mappings, use `sa_` as the right hand side in your example instead of `ys_`.",
